{"parentUuid":"fe994444-7867-4c2f-aade-7a3b61683e2c","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"e83b6a4f-63a8-4fe4-afcd-e7857787d75e","agentId":"ae7f316477361ec0a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UJ17ZnXVTK6vJX9inXGxKf","type":"tool_result","content":"=== review_supertraining_ch5a_opus.md\n## Overall verdict\n\n**GO AFTER FIXES.** Required fixes:\n\n1. Newton II: flag ΔV as final velocity (equals change only from rest); \"net propulsive impulse\"; replace circular-motion example in (d) with constant-gravity projectile; \"net external force on the body\" in (c).\n2. Dynamic correspondence: fix \"paragraph before\" to \"paragraph that closes\" the dynamics discussion; label \"This passage is the authors' own statement ... Use it when\" as Inference.\n3. Three methods: say which load-rep pairing clashes (90-95%/3-6 clearly; 85-95%/3-5RM loosely); rewrite the line-105 fragment with an \"Eric's baseline:\" prefix.\n4. DeLorme: remove or label \"mostly in rehabilitation or untrained subjects\".\n5. Berger: correct the traceability sentence (conclusions 1 and 5 trace to Berger 1963 on p.259; only 6 is orphaned); add the 1-3 rep advanced-lifter sentence.\n6. Ivanov: retitle and rename (eccentric raised squat 1RM most; no \"own test\" for eccentric); label the \"trains the nervous system for that mode\" gloss.\n7. Implement mass: retitle and rename away from \"stay close to competition mass\"; fix When to apply; add the far-from-competition counterexamples (labelled Inference).\n8. After renames in 6 and 7, update inbound wikilinks in this batch.\n\nNo NO-GO. Both `contested` entries keep both sides on the cited pages. The single `proven` entry keeps its scope.\n=== review_supertraining_ch5b_opus.md\n## Overall verdict\n\n**GO AFTER FIXES.** Required fixes:\n1. high-volume: change `contested` to `supported`; point to the brief-maximal-tension entry for the conflict.\n2. surface-footwear: change `contested` to `supported`; rewrite the tension as different aims.\n3. strength-endurance-ceiling: drop rowers from the conflict; correct the glycolytic inference using baseline line 117.\n4. brief-maximal-tension: add the line-76 DSI tag verbatim; fix the \"jumping from depth\" Example; add the novice-sequencing caveat and link.\n5. 475-jumps: add the novice-sequencing caveat and link; title \"tons\".\n6. depth-jump-height: correct the mRSI baseline statement (readiness marker, line 74); add the Ch4 p.222 locator for \"considerably lower\".\n7. volume-and-rest: move item 1 and \"1-15 min\" out of the depth-jump model (Fig 5.11 shows ground jumps); label voices (Siff vs Verkhoshansky 1977).\n8. five-phases: soften the EM-delay \"conflict\" to a wording difference.\n9. classification and momentum-intensity: change the voice to Siff for the powermetrics passages.\n10. Lewis: take the Inference out of the title or label it; mark line 77 as Inferred.\n11. injury-risk: quote the PDF 281 margin-cut words as printed (\"adequ[ate]\", \"running a[nd] jumping\").\n12. resisted-water: quote the \"No resistance methods should not use\" double negative as printed.\n=== review_supertraining_ch5a_opus_round2.md\n## Overall verdict\n\n**GO AFTER FIXES.** One required fix:\n\n1. `claim--implement-mass-for-speed-strength-keep-technique-and-size-per-athlete.md`, When NOT: replace \"only the shot and baseball data fit it\" as given above (the 57 g light baseball is -61% of the 148 g regulation ball on PDF 276; Egstrom measured precision).\n\nThe other 18 entries can be promoted as they stand. The single `proven` entry keeps its identity-only scope; both `contested` entries keep both sides on the cited pages. Optional nits (non-blocking): the Newton closing list should include (a); the Berger traceability sentence could carry \"Inference:\"; the loading entry's \"closes on two levers\" could read \"summary names two levers\".\n=== review_supertraining_ch5b_opus_round2.md\n## Overall verdict\n\n**GO AFTER FIXES.** Two one-line fixes:\n1. `claim--depth-jump-training-beat-higher-volume-traditional-training-in-jumpers.md`: change \"untested for novices\" to \"not supported for novices\".\n2. `heuristic--depth-jump-weekly-frequency-and-seasonal-placement.md`: tag the line 105 citation \"Inferred (transcript + shared slides); the baseline adds \\\"Not claimed in the interview\\\"\".\n\nAfter those two, the batch is ready to promote. Neither needs another full review round; a grep confirming both strings is enough.\n=== review_supertraining_ch5c_opus_round2.md\n## Overall verdict\n\n**GO AFTER FIXES.** 25 GO, 1 FIX, 0 NO-GO.\n\nRequired fix:\n1. `heuristic--allow-restoration-after-a-concentrated-block-before-the-next.md`: Bompa & Haff locator to PDF idx 60 / printed p. 49; label the \"matches neither\" judgment as Inference, note the alternative reading, and add Bompa & Haff's magnitude-and-duration sentence (exact text in the table).\n\nAlso required (not an entry): correct the \"Vault follow-up for Eric\" in `staging/fixes_supertraining_ch5c_applied.md` so it no longer says the \"longer loading, longer delay\" rule is in neither book, and fix its idx 61 locator.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"6bbb0116-52ce-48f4-9fc7-231c0e6cca08","timestamp":"2026-10-03T18:07:16.053Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"=== review_supertraining_ch5a_opus.md\n## Overall verdict\n\n**GO AFTER FIXES.** Required fixes:\n\n1. Newton II: flag ΔV as final velocity (equals change only from rest); \"net propulsive impulse\"; replace circular-motion example in (d) with constant-gravity projectile; \"net external force on the body\" in (c).\n2. Dynamic correspondence: fix \"paragraph before\" to \"paragraph that closes\" the dynamics discussion; label \"This passage is the authors' own statement ... Use it when\" as Inference.\n3. Three methods: say which load-rep pairing clashes (90-95%/3-6 clearly; 85-95%/3-5RM loosely); rewrite the line-105 fragment with an \"Eric's baseline:\" prefix.\n4. DeLorme: remove or label \"mostly in rehabilitat