{"parentUuid":"9e950523-56b9-4bf5-92af-ec2aea0078b4","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"e83b6a4f-63a8-4fe4-afcd-e7857787d75e","agentId":"ae7f316477361ec0a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Mt3xnTwyaSYWY9Zhqp1rrT","type":"tool_result","content":"##### block-periodization--issurin/heuristic--nine-step-annual-program-construction-sequence.md\nchapter: \"4.1\"\nconfidence: supported\n**What it is** — Issurin gives a fixed nine-step sequence for constructing an annual\n##### block-periodization--issurin/claim--multi-peak-annual-preparation-elite-track-and-field.md\nchapter: \"1.1.3\"\nconfidence: supported\n**What it is** — Table 1.5 (PDF p. 24, printed p. 13, based on Suslov, 2001, with Issurin's\n##### block-periodization--issurin/framework--training-stage-and-multi-peak-annual-cycle.md\nchapter: \"1.2.3\"\nconfidence: supported\n**What it is** — Issurin's annual cycle is built from a sequence of **training stages**,\n##### periodization--bompa/heuristic--fatigue-fitness-3to1-ratio.md\nchapter: \"1\"\nconfidence: supported\n**What it is** — Zatsiorsky and Kraemer (cited by Bompa) propose that the fatigue from a training bout dissipates roughly **three times faster** than the positive training effect persists — e.g., fatigue lasts ~24 hr while the fitness benefit lasts ~72 hr. The positive effect only becomes *visible* once the masking fatigue has cleared; adaptation and improved performance surface afterward.\n##### periodization--bompa/framework--step-loading-paradigm.md\nchapter: \"2\"\nconfidence: proven\n**What it is** — The classic periodization loading model: training load rises in a *wavelike* pattern across microcycles rather than continuously. The canonical form is **3:1** — load increases across three microcycles (weeks), then drops in a fourth unloading week for regeneration before the next series begins. Variants scale to the athlete: **4:2** (four loading weeks, two unloading) for more advanced work, **2:1** for younger or less-trained athletes. Because a single session can't drive noticeable adaptation, the load is held across a microcycle, then stepped up.\n/Users/kristinarash/SecondBrain/Knowledge/library/research-papers/issurin-2016-benefits-and-limitations-of-block-periodized-training-approaches-to-athletes-preparation-a.md\n/Users/kristinarash/SecondBrain/Knowledge/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky/heuristic--sequence-jumps-then-barbell-then-depth-jumps-across-stages.md\n/Users/kristinarash/SecondBrain/Knowledge/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky/framework--conjugate-sequence-system-of-training-means.md\n/Users/kristinarash/SecondBrain/Knowledge/library/strength-and-conditioning/block-periodization--issurin/framework--transmutation-mesocycle-duration-and-overtraining-monitoring.md\n/Users/kristinarash/SecondBrain/Knowledge/library/strength-and-conditioning/block-periodization--issurin/framework--accumulation-mesocycle-duration-and-monitoring.md\n/Users/kristinarash/SecondBrain/Knowledge/library/strength-and-conditioning/block-periodization--issurin/principle--concentration-of-training-workloads.md\n/Users/kristinarash/SecondBrain/Knowledge/library/strength-and-conditioning/block-periodization--issurin/framework--training-stage-and-multi-peak-annual-cycle.md\n/Users/kristinarash/SecondBrain/Knowledge/library/strength-and-conditioning/block-periodization--issurin/framework--realization-mesocycle-taper-prescription.md\n/Users/kristinarash/SecondBrain/Knowledge/library/strength-and-conditioning/block-periodization--issurin/framework--prolonging-residual-effects-with-mini-blocks.md\n/Users/kristinarash/SecondBrain/Knowledge/library/strength-and-conditioning/block-periodization--issurin/_book.md","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"8fd92a75-cb5b-4ecb-9ce2-abea7dd949c8","timestamp":"2026-10-03T18:10:43.189Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"##### block-periodization--issurin/heuristic--nine-step-annual-program-construction-sequence.md\nchapter: \"4.1\"\nconfidence: supported\n**What it is** — Issurin gives a fixed nine-step sequence for constructing an annual\n##### block-periodization--issurin/claim--multi-peak-annual-preparation-elite-track-and-field.md\nchapter: \"1.1.3\"\nconfidence: supported\n**What it is** — Table 1.5 (PDF p. 24, printed p. 13, based on Suslov, 2001, with Issurin's\n##### block-periodization--issurin/framework--training-stage-and-multi-peak-annual-cycle.md\nchapter: \"1.2.3\"\nconfidence: supported\n**What it is** — Issurin's annual cycle is built from a sequence of **training stages**,\n##### periodization--bompa/heuristic--fatigue-fitness-3to1-ratio.md\nchapter: \"1\"\nconfidence: supported\n**What it is** — Zatsiorsky and Kraemer (cited by Bompa) propose that the fatigue from a training bout dissipates roughly **three times faster** than the positive training effect persists — e.g., fatigue lasts ~24 hr while the fitness benefit lasts ~72 hr. The positive effect only becomes *visible* once the masking fatigue has cleared; adaptation and improved performance surface afterward.\n##### periodization--bompa/framework--step-loading-paradigm.md\nchapter: \"2\"\nconfidence: proven\n**What it is** — The classic periodization loading model: training load rises in a *wavelike* pattern across microcycles rather than continuously. The canonical form is **3:1** — load increases across three microcycles (weeks), then drops in a fourth unloading week for regeneration before the next series begins. Variants scale to the athlete: **4:2** (four loading weeks, two unloading) for more advanced work, **2:1** for younger or less-trained athletes. Because a single session can't drive noticeable adaptation, the load is held across a microcycle, then stepped up.\n/Users/kristinarash/SecondBrain/Knowledge/library/research-papers/issurin-2016-benefits-and-limitations-of-block-periodized-training-approaches-to-athletes-preparation-a.md\n/Users/kristinarash/SecondBrain/Knowledge/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky/heuristic--sequence-jumps-then-barbell-then-depth-jumps-across-stages.md\n/Users/kristinarash/SecondBrain/Knowledge/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky/framework--conjugate-sequence-system-of-training-means.md\n/Users/kristinarash/SecondBrain/Knowledge/library/strength-and-conditioning/block-periodization--issurin/framework--transmutation-mesocycle-duration-and-overtraining-monitoring.md\n/Users/kristinarash/SecondBrain/Knowledge/library/strength-and-conditioning/block-periodization--issurin/framework--accumulation-mesocycle-duration-and-monitoring.md\n/Users/kristinarash/SecondBrain/Knowledge/library/strength-and-conditioning/block-periodization--issurin/principle--concentration-of-training-workloads.md\n/Users/kristinarash/SecondBrain/Knowledge/library/strength-and-conditioning/block-periodization--issurin/framework--training-stage-and-multi-peak-annual-cycle.md\n/Users/kristinarash/SecondBrain/Knowledge/library/strength-and-conditioning/block-periodization--issurin/framework--realization-mesocycle-taper-prescription.md\n/Users/kristinarash/SecondBrain/Knowledge/library/strength-and-conditioning/block-periodization--issurin/framework--prolonging-residual-effects-with-mini-blocks.md\n/Users/kristinarash/SecondBrain/Knowledge/library/strength-and-conditioning/block-periodization--issurin/_book.md","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9e950523-56b9-4bf5-92af-ec2aea0078b4","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"supertraining-ch4-3-4"}
