work--speed-sport-block-organisation-and-two-glycolytic-peaks.md","description":"Fix baseline line number"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CffmS9KtfoWsovnDnoV8n","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"84cf9678-b980-4071-b1c4-b53328b49c13","timestamp":"2026-10-03T18:21:01.343Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"supertraining-ch4-3-4"}
{"parentUuid":"84cf9678-b980-4071-b1c4-b53328b49c13","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"e83b6a4f-63a8-4fe4-afcd-e7857787d75e","agentId":"ae7f316477361ec0a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01B7hrByWNpaSETwsu62EJzW","type":"tool_result","content":"line 116, Explicit, claimed again as Explicit (interview 2026-09-28, Q1\nline 117, Explicit (interview 2026-09-28, Q19\nline 116 is about in-season emphasis. No volumes, durations or intensities are given for either glycolytic peak.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"47915734-7d51-4504-95d1-58dc0c4bef15","timestamp":"2026-10-03T18:21:01.689Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"line 116, Explicit, claimed again as Explicit (interview 2026-09-28, Q1\nline 117, Explicit (interview 2026-09-28, Q19\nline 116 is about in-season emphasis. No volumes, durations or intensities are given for either glycolytic peak.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky/framework--speed-sport-block-organisation-and-two-glycolytic-peaks.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":23,"oldLines":9,"newStart":23,"newLines":9,"lines":[" "," **Why it works** — The authors give the reason for allowing coordination work during the block (it is compatible with a lowered functional state) and for the maintenance dose (explosive strength falls during the second glycolytic peak). They do not explain why speed must be excluded entirely rather than reduced. Inference: it follows from their rule that high-intensity work needs a fresh, not a depressed, functional state ([[heuristic--technique-work-during-and-after-a-concentrated-strength-block]])."," ","-**When to apply** — Cyclic speed sports such as sprinting, and by the authors' mention of \"team sports\" for the second glycolytic peak, sports where repeated speed matters. Eric's baseline: \"For football specifically, the stated priority stack is: Goal 1, alactic and aerobic capacity/power for fall-camp demands; Goal 2, the same two systems for game demands; glycolytic conditioning is treated as a \\\"worst case scenario\\\" to be absorbed incidentally through camp and practice rather than programmed as a primary target\" (`docs/method-baseline.md`, line 115, Explicit, claimed again as Explicit (interview 2026-09-28, Q1)). Inference: the authors program two deliberate glycolytic peaks, which goes further than the baseline; their own caution (small segments combined with speed work, a maintenance dose for explosive strength) is the part that fits the baseline best.","+**When to apply** — Cyclic speed sports such as sprinting, and by the authors' mention of \"team sports\" for the second glycolytic peak, sports where repeated speed matters. Eric's baseline: \"For football specifically, the stated priority stack is: Goal 1, alactic and aerobic capacity/power for fall-camp demands; Goal 2, the same two systems for game demands; glycolytic conditioning is treated as a \\\"worst case scenario\\\" to be absorbed incidentally through camp and practice rather than programmed as a primary target\" (`docs/method-baseline.md`, line 116, Explicit, claimed again as Explicit (interview 2026-09-28, Q1)). Inference: the authors program two deliberate glycolytic peaks, which goes further than the baseline; their own caution (small segments combined with speed work, a maintenance dose for explosive strength) is the part that fits the baseline best."," ","-**When NOT to apply** — Speed-strength and complex-technical sports keep some technique and do not separate speed so sharply ([[framework--bi-cyclic-annual-model-for-explosive-strength-sports]]). Eric's baseline also says \"staff do program it in the off-season\" for glycolytic work (line 117, Explicit (interview 2026-09-28, Q19)), so the conflict with line 115 is about in-season emphasis. No volumes, durations or intensities are given for either glycolytic peak.","+**When NOT to apply** — Speed-strength and complex-technical sports keep some technique and do not separate speed so sharply ([[framework--bi-cyclic-annual-model-for-explosive-strength-sports]]). Eric's baseline also says \"staff do program it in the off-season\" for glycolytic work (line 117, Explicit (interview 2026-09-28, Q19)), so the conflict with line 116 is about in-season emphasis. No volumes, durations or intensities are given for either glycolytic peak."," "," **Example** — The authors give the schematic only. Inference: a 200 m sprinter spends a concentrated strength block doing strength-endurance circuits and relaxed technical drills with no sprinting, starts sprint work as the block ends, and adds short speed-endurance runs only after sprint volume has peaked, with a few explosive lifts kept in each week."," "]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky/framework--speed-sport-block-organisation-and-two-glycolytic-peaks.md"]}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"84cf9678-b980-4071-b1c4-b53328b49c13","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"supertraining-ch4-3-4"}
