{"parentUuid":"0534e374-2467-4435-9d25-618711952a93","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ae7f316477361ec0a","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CffnPzHygZwxZfmtcGXo4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote 25 new entries covering all of batch 6d: sections 6.12 to 6.17, PDF 379-403 (printed 368-392). I stopped at the end of Chapter 6, as asked. Lint flags none of the 25 files. No existing entry, `_book.md` or vault file was edited, and no git was run.\n\n**By kind and confidence**\n- 9 frameworks: 8 `supported`, 1 `contested`\n- 6 heuristics: all `supported`\n- 4 claims: 3 `contested`, 1 `supported`\n- 3 case studies: 2 `supported`, 1 `untested` (the Tabachnik sprinter norms)\n- 3 principles: all `supported`\n\nThat makes 4 `contested`, 20 `supported`, 1 `untested`, and no `proven`. Three of the four `contested` entries name Issurin 2016, which found too little evidence for concentrated, single-emphasis loading in team, combat and swimming preparation. They are the explosive-strength model, the concentrated-strength claim and the complex-training claim. The fourth, the bi-cyclic claim, is contested inside the book: aim 1 (PDF 389) calls for two large mesocycles even in monocyclic sports, but PDF 387 and 396 recommend a monocycle for long-duration endurance. It also names Issurin's stage length (about 2 months, 4-7 per season).\n\n**6.14.1, the explosive-strength model** (`framework--bi-cyclic-annual-model-for-explosive-strength-sports.md`). I read Fig 6.39 at 300 dpi. Every month value is \"about\", because phase boundaries do not fall on the month ticks:\n- Phases: I is months 1-4, II month 5, III months 6-8, IV months 9-11.\n- Strength blocks: block 1 covers months 1-3; block 2 covers months 6-7 and is about two thirds as tall.\n- Fitness curves: two upper curves cross around months 8-9, so only the end order is certain (Starting, then Explosive, then Maximum strength).\n- Training means: the GPP and Speed curves cannot be told apart in the image, so I took GPP's timing from the text.\n- Fig 6.38 (jumps, then weights, then depth jumps inside one block, with weights the largest) is folded into this entry rather than written up separately.\n\n**Entries per section, for `_book.md`**\n\n| Section | Printed pages | PDF pages | Entries |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 6.12 lead and 6.12.1 | 368 | 379 | 1 |\n| 6.12.2 | 368-373 | 379-384 | 6 |\n| 6.12.3 | 374-378 | 385-389 | 4 |\n| 6.13 | 378-379 | 389-390 | 1 |\n| 6.14 lead and tables | 379-382 | 390-393 | 2 |\n| 6.14.1 | 383-384 | 394-395 | 1 |\n| 6.14.2-6.14.3 | 384-386 | 395-397 | 2 |\n| 6.14.4 (with \"More Advanced Use\") | 386-388 | 397-399 | 3 |\n| 6.14.5 | 389 | 400 | 1 |\n| 6.15 | 389-390 | 400-401 | 1 |\n| 6.16 | 391-392 | 402-403 | 2 |\n| 6.17 | 392 | 403 | 1 |\n\nThe paragraph above the 6.12 heading on PDF 379 is the end of 6.11. I quote it, located as 6.11, in the programme-objective entry.\n\n**What I read and couldn't read**\n- I opened every page from PDF 379 to 392 and 394 to 403 as an image, plus a 300 dpi crop of Fig 6.39.\n- PDF 393 (Tables 6.10-6.12) I read from the text layer only, and I cite no number from it.\n- Nothing was unreadable.\n\n**Unclear or contradictory spots (all recorded in the entries, none resolved)**\n- **Fig 6.45 and 6.46:** the captions say \"A is the block of concentrated strength loading\", but the figures print \"GPP\" under A and \"Strength Load\" under B.\n- **Fig 6.36(b) text vs figure:** the text says anaerobic productivity \"exceeded its initial level after 72 hours\", but the curve crosses 100% at about 30-36 h. That curve is labelled \"Training effect\", not anaerobic.\n- **Fig 6.36(b) aerobic curve:** the text says aerobic potential \"diminished\" after 12 h, but the figure still shows it about 6% above initial at 72 h.\n- **Author spelling:** the figure caption says \"Kubelin, 1980\"; the text (PDF 381, 388) says \"Kudelin\".\n- **Table 6.8 splits:** 5.70 + 4.45 = 10.15 s against a 10.0 s goal, and 6.15 + 5.00 = 11.15 s against 11.0 s. Table 6.9 gives 4.30-4.40 s for the second 50 m, faster than Table 6.8's 4.45 s.\n- **PDF 381, same page:** concentrated loading lasts \"up to 2 months\", but unidirectional stages run \"4-12 weeks\".\n- **Volume savings:** 13-15% (annual strength volume, PDF 382) vs 20% (all training volume over a macrocycle, PDF 305). I recorded these as different quantities, not a contradiction.\n- **Minor:** \"phase B\" is printed that way on PDF 398, and Table 6.7's caption refers to \"Table 6.8\" strength tests.\n\n**Overlap with the parallel 6.9-6.11 batch.** Two of its files, both now on disk, cover similar ground to two of mine:\n- `heuristic--time-technique-and-competition-strength-work-to-the-ldte-window` (6.10) overlaps my technique heuristic.\n- `principle--long-term-delayed-training-effect-from-volume-above-the-optimum` (6.10) overlaps my loading-reduction heuristic.\n\nI linked each from the matching entry and said what the 6.12.2 pages add. Those two files may be renamed in their own review, so the links may need updating.\n\n**Reciprocal-link suggestions** (other entry first, then which of mine it should link to):\n- Ch5 `framework--conjugate-sequence-system-of-training-means` and `framework--conditions-for-concentrated-unidirectional-loading`: the 6.14.1 model and `claim--concentrated-strength-loading-limited-period-qualified-athletes-and-volume-saving`.\n- Ch5 `heuristic--allow-restoration-after-a-concentrated-block-before-the-next`: `heuristic--loading-reduction-for-the-delayed-effect-must-outlast-1-2-weeks`.\n- Ch5 `claim--excess-heavy-strength-volume-impairs-speed-strength-and-technique`: the Antonova and Levchenko case study.\n- Ch5 `heuristic--sequence-jumps-then-barbell-then-depth-jumps-across-stages`: the 6.14.1 model (Fig 6.38).\n- Vault Issurin `heuristic--nine-step-annual-program-construction-sequence` and Evans `framework--ten-step-process-for-building-an-annual-plan`: the eight-step framework.\n- Vault Bondarchuk `claim--model-characteristic-tables-exist-by-qualification`: the Tabachnik case study.\n- Vault Bompa `framework--step-loading-paradigm`: the loading-reduction heuristic. This is recorded as a tension (a 3:1 deload vs \"far longer than 1-2 weeks\"), not a contradiction.\n- The two parallel-batch 6.10 files above: my technique and loading-reduction heuristics.\n\n**Lint output.** These are the only lines; neither is from my files:\n```\nsupertraining--verkhoshansky/_book.md: body em dash lines [12, 132, 133]\nTOTAL ISSUES: 1\n```\n\nAll 25 entries are in `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky/`. Page renders are `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/_renders/6d_p*.png`.\n\nFiles are in `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/`:\n- `_scope_supertraining_ch6d.txt`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":422,"cache_read_input_tokens":346463,"output_tokens":2847,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":422},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2847,"cache_read_input_tokens":346463,"cache_creation_input_tokens":422,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":422,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CffnPaiuD3CC7ZMf1cDRK","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"dfbe0d59-7d92-4910-81aa-76738826f23c","timestamp":"2026-10-03T18:33:41.739Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/F